course: dictionary
lesson: 8064
title: One word, many meanings: relative
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word relative can mean different things, so context tells you which meaning is right. «Dad's mother is Mum's mother-in-law, a relative by marriage.» Here a relative is a person in your family, like a grandmother or an aunt.
explain: As an adjective, relative means compared with something else. In «relative size», you measure how big something is by comparing it with something else. «That was Paraceratherium, a hornless relative of rhinos» means a creature closely linked to rhinos, a bit like a cousin in the animal world.
explain: Try swapping your meaning into the sentence. If «a distant relative» means a family member who is further away, does «The porcupines are only distant relatives» still make sense? It does, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A relative (noun) is a person in your family, like an aunt, uncle, cousin or grandparent.
fact: A close relative is someone very near to you in your family; a distant relative is further away.
fact: Relative (adjective) means compared with something else, as in «relative size» or «relative to» something.
fact: In grammar, a relative pronoun (who, which or that) joins a clause to a noun, as in «the girl who waved».
fact: «Relative» can be a noun or an adjective, so check the sentence to see which one it is.
exercise: «Dad's mother is Mum's mother-in-law, a relative by marriage.» In this sentence, what is a relative? | A grammar word that joins clauses | *A person in your family | A type of petrol station | A kind of rock
exercise: What does relative mean in «relative size»? | A member of your family | Very large | A word like who or which | *Compared with something else
exercise: In «the girl who waved at me», which word is the relative pronoun? | waved | the | *who | girl
test: «The American and the African and Asian porcupines are only distant relatives.» What does distant suggest? | Very tall and thin | Lost forever | Living right next door | *Not very closely related
test: Which sentence uses relative as an adjective? | My cousin is my relative | The woodlouse is a relative of crabs | *The dog looked small relative to the horse | The rock hyrax has elephants as relatives
exam: In «a woodlouse with fourteen legs is not an insect either, it is a relative of crabs», what is the woodlouse a relative of? | Porcupines | Insects | *Crabs | Rhinos
